% Pure OAuth transport and signed OpenID identity
Own pdd/chatgpt_oauth.py. Extract the OAuth transport, constants, switch check,
and signature validation from chatgpt_sign_in, without changing behavior. Use
existing cryptography and Python built-ins. This removes the runtime import cycle.
R1: request_json sends form data only to fixed official endpoints, refuses redirects,
bounds responses and returns safe errors, never raw provider content.
R2: verify_identity accepts RS256/ES256 only; fixed official JWKS, key/algorithm
match; validate issuer, issued-client audience/azp, exp, iat, optional nbf, nonce,
and nonempty subject. Reject malformed signatures/claims. Inject JWKS/time for tests.
R3: require_enabled enforces literal PDD_CHATGPT_SIGN_IN=1. Signature checks are
pure and do not require opt-in. No credential storage or browser launch here.
References: https://developers.openai.com/siwc/token-sharing-open-source/sign-in
https://developers.openai.com/siwc/website
